{
  "an8.14:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 8.14 ",
  "an8.14:0.2": "2. The Great Chapter ",
  "an8.14:0.3": "A Wild Colt ",
  "an8.14:1.1": "“Mendicants, I will teach you about eight wild colts and eight defects in horses, and about eight wild people and eight defects in people. ",
  "an8.14:1.2": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "an8.14:1.3": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "an8.14:1.4": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "an8.14:2.1": "“And what, mendicants, are the eight wild colts and eight defects in horses? ",
  "an8.14:2.2": "Firstly, when the trainer says ‘giddyup!’ and spurs and goads them on, some wild colts back right up and spin the chariot behind them. ",
  "an8.14:2.3": "Some wild colts are like that. ",
  "an8.14:2.4": "This is the first defect of a horse. ",
  "an8.14:3.1": "Furthermore, when the trainer says ‘giddyup!’ and spurs and goads them on, some wild colts jump back, wreck the hub, and break the triple rod. ",
  "an8.14:3.2": "Some wild colts are like that. ",
  "an8.14:3.3": "This is the second defect of a horse. ",
  "an8.14:4.1": "Furthermore, when the trainer says ‘giddyup!’ and spurs and goads them on, some wild colts shake the draft-pole off their thigh and trample it. ",
  "an8.14:4.2": "Some wild colts are like that. ",
  "an8.14:4.3": "This is the third defect of a horse. ",
  "an8.14:5.1": "Furthermore, when the trainer says ‘giddyup!’ and spurs and goads them on, some wild colts take a wrong turn, sending the chariot off track. ",
  "an8.14: